    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the GPS trace for TRP-00103 is 11.18 km against the booked optimal route of 8.2 km, an excess of 2.98 km or 36.3%. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so a deviation is established — but it is not a MATERIAL deviation, since it is below the 8.0 km and 50% marks.\n\nThe LTA DataMall closure on Braddell Road (active 05:30–12:00 on the trip date) names a road the optimal route uses, covers the 08:07–08:36 trace window with far more than the 15-minute buffer, and the driver left the corridor before the affected stretch and rejoined it after. Under POL-RD-03 the whole measured excess falls within the exoneration cap of 1.30 x (10.6 − 8.2) + 1.00 = 4.12 km, since 2.98 km is the lesser figure. The excess is therefore fully exonerated, nothing remains to refund on distance, and the distance and time charges stand.\n\nThe ERP is a separate line. The route the rider booked carries no gantry at all (optimal_route_erp_sgd 0.00), yet the fare ledger bills two CTE gantries — S$3.00 and S$1.00, both flagged on_optimal_route false. Because the detour is excused as an external event, POL-RD-09(2) refunds off-route ERP to the rider as a standalone pass-through correction, capped at S$12.00. S$4.00 is due. Under POL-RD-09(1) this S$4.00 is never added on top of a distance refund — and there is no distance refund here — so it is the whole of the rider's recovery.\n\nOn evidence handling: the trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (175 fixes at the expected 10-second interval, coverage_pct 100.0, empty gaps array, max_gap_sec 0.0), so none of the POL-RD-07 limbs fires and no independent corroboration was required. Every artifact carried weight_multiplier 1.0, so no disclosure or discount applied. Both gantry lines correspond to fixes on the trace, so they are genuine pass-through charges and not phantom lines; no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral arises, and no POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral arises because the driver shows no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 553 completed trips). No escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 is present.\n\nOutcome: the rider's claim is partly upheld. S$4.00 of the disputed amount is refunded; the balance of the fare stands.",
